  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A short scroll bound with a gold cord that has no knot. The writing inside is a single sentence, and people who have seen one say that the sentence was shorter than they expected.</p><p><strong>Read the Scroll.</strong> As an action, you read the scroll and cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWish000000]{Wish}, whatever your class and without a check. The scroll is used up, and you suffer none of the stress the spell normally causes its caster.</p><p><strong>Written Once.</strong> The scroll holds exactly the words its scribe wrote, and the scribe chose them. Whoever commissions it decides the wording with the scribe at the desk; whoever reads it gets that wish and no other. A careless clause is the reader's to live with.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
